    "category": "😃 Smileys & People",
    "description": "A yellow face with closed eyes, furrowed eyebrows, broad frown, and two puffs of steam blowing out of its nose, as if in a huff or fuming. , May convey various negative emotions, including irritation, anger, and contempt. May also convey feelings of pride, dominance, and empowerment. , Originally named Face With Look of Triumph, and the steam from its nose may derive from a visual shorthand for frustration or disdain in anime and manga. , Samsung’s design previously looked like its head was titled back in a more arrogant expression. Earlier designs from Microsoft depicted a big, open mouth without steam and from Facebook, a smiley that resembled 😬 Grimacing Face., , Face With Steam From Nose was approved as part of Unicode 6.0 in 2010, under the name “Face With Look of Triumph”, and added to Emoji 1.0 in 2015.",
