    "emoji": "🐩",
    "category": "🐻 Animals & Nature",
    "description": "A poodle, a popular dog breed with curly hair, often groomed in an ornamental pattern., Generally depicted as a grayish-white poodle in full profile on all fours facing left, with a shaved torso, legs, and face with fuller, pom-pom-like hair on its head, ears, chest, feet, and tip of tail (as the Continental Clip)., Like 🐕 Dog, may be used to represent a variety of dog breeds (often fluffy or long-haired). See also 🐶 Dog Face., With an upturned snout, Google’s poodle bears an endearingly haughty expression., Google, Samsung, and Facebook’s design previously featured pink poodles., , Poodle was approved as part of Unicode 6.0 in 2010, and added to Emoji 1.0 in 2015.",
