    "description": "A rosette, a stylized, flower-shaped decoration often presented as an award with a ribbon or (military) medal. Appears as a motif in ancient culptures. Generally depicted as a circular, yellow-and-orange flower., Commonly used for Valentine’s Day, Mother’s Day, and other special occasions. May be more generally used to express such ideas as love, happiness, and beauty. Also used as a yellow accent color., Not to be confused with 🌼 Blossom, though their applications may overlap., WhatsApp's rosette is orange, white, and purple; Twitter's is purple and blue. Samsung's was previously pink., , Rosette was approved as part of Unicode 7.0 in 2014, and added to Emoji 1.0 in 2015.",
